<p style="margin:0;font-weight:600">Theatre Nurse (Scrub) — nights, 3 months</p>
<p style="margin:2px 0 14px;color:#555">Candidate C-4471</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 4px">Eleven years scrub experience across two NHS trusts, currently working nights, and available at two weeks' notice.</p>
<p style="margin:18px 0 6px;font-weight:600">Against the brief</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 0 18px;padding:0">
<li style="margin:0 0 6px"><strong>NMC registration, current:</strong> Holds current NMC registration, renewed this year.<sup>[1]</sup></li>
<li style="margin:0 0 6px"><strong>Scrub experience in orthopaedics:</strong> Eight years scrub in orthopaedic theatres, including primary and revision arthroplasty.<sup>[2]</sup></li>
<li style="margin:0 0 6px"><strong>Night shift availability:</strong> Has worked a permanent night rota for the last two years.<sup>[3]</sup></li>
</ul>
<p style="margin:18px 0 6px;font-weight:600">What we know about your process</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 0 18px;padding:0">
<li style="margin:0 0 6px">The trust interviews with the theatre manager and a senior scrub nurse together, so expect a clinical scenario rather than a competency grid.<sup>[4]</sup></li>
<li style="margin:0 0 6px">They turned down the last candidate for not asking about the on-call arrangement, so brief this one to raise it.<sup>[5]</sup></li>
</ul>
<p style="margin:18px 0 6px;font-weight:600">Where they don't meet the brief</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 0 18px;padding:0">
<li style="margin:0 0 6px">No documented paediatric theatre experience, which the brief lists as desirable.<sup>[6]</sup></li>
</ul>
<p style="margin:18px 0 6px;font-weight:600">For the recruiter to confirm before sending</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 0 18px;padding:0">
<li style="margin:0 0 6px">Confirm the candidate can start on the 11th rather than the 18th.</li>
<li style="margin:0 0 6px">Check whether the trust requires a separate scrub competency sign-off.</li>
</ul>
